Let $\mathcal{M}=(\mathcal{M},I,\otimes)$ be a metatheory.
We define the (locally large) 2-category ${\mathscr{M}\!\mathscr{M}\!od(\mathcal{M})}$ of 
metamodels of $\mathcal{M}$ as follows.
\begin{itemize}
\item An object is a metamodel 
$(\mathcal{C},\Phi,\overline{\phi}_\cdot,\overline{\phi})$ of $\mathcal{M}$.
\item A 1-cell from $(\mathcal{C},\Phi,\overline{\phi}_\cdot,\overline{\phi})$ to 
$(\mathcal{C'},\Phi',\overline{\phi'}_\cdot,\overline{\phi'})$
is a functor $G\colon \mathcal{C}\longrightarrow \mathcal{C'}$
together with a natural transformation $(g_{X,A,B}\colon 
\Phi_X(A,B)\longrightarrow \Phi'_X(GA,GB))_{X\in\mathcal{M},A,B\in\mathcal{C}}$ 
making the following 
diagrams commute for all 
\begin{comment}




































\end{comment}
$X,Y\in\mathcal{M}$ and $A,B,C\in\mathcal{C}$:
\begin{equation*}
\begin{tikzpicture}[baseline=-\the\dimexpr\fontdimen22\textfont2\relax ]
