\label{cor:enrichr_olactl_equiv}
Let $\mathcal{M}$ be a metatheory.
\begin{enumerate}
\item The 2-functors in Proposition~\ref{prop:enrichment_as_metamodel}
and Proposition~\ref{prop:oplax_action_as_metamodel} restrict to 
fully faithful 2-functors 
\[
{\mathscr{E}\!nrich^{\mathrm{r}}(\mathcal{M})}\longrightarrow{\mathscr{M}\!\mathscr{M}\!od(\mathcal{M})}\qquad
{\mathscr{A}\!ct^{\mathrm{l}}_{\mathrm{oplax}}(\mathcal{M})}\longrightarrow{\mathscr{M}\!\mathscr{M}\!od(\mathcal{M})}
\]
with the same essential image characterised as follows:
a metamodel $(\mathcal{C},\Phi,\overline{\phi}_\cdot,\overline{\phi})$ 
of $\mathcal{M}$ is in the essential image if and only if
for each $X\in\mathcal{M}$ and $A,B\in\mathcal{C}$,
the functors 
\[
\Phi_{(-)}(A,B)\colon\mathcal{M}^{\mathrm{op}}\longrightarrow\mathbf{SET}\qquad
\Phi_X(A,-)\colon\mathcal{C}\longrightarrow\mathbf{SET}
\] 
are representable.
\item The 2-categories ${\mathscr{E}\!nrich^{\mathrm{r}}(\mathcal{M})}$ and ${\mathscr{A}\!ct^{\mathrm{l}}_{\mathrm{oplax}}(\mathcal{M})}$ are 
equivalent.
\end{enumerate}

\label{def:morphism_of_metatheories}
Let $\mathcal{M}=(\mathcal{M},I_\mathcal{M},\otimes_\mathcal{M})$ and 
$\mathcal{N}=(\mathcal{N},I_\mathcal{N},\otimes_\mathcal{N})$ be metatheories. 
A \textbf{morphism of metatheories from $\mathcal{M}$ to $\mathcal{N}$} 
is a lax monoidal functor 
\[
